# mkosi applies presets to the whole image, and Debian's presets enable anything
# not listed. Off: Debian's per-cluster WAL archiving and dump templates; backups
# are ours to schedule (D2), and an unconfigured pg_receivewal fails at every boot.
disable pg_*
# Weekly TRIM, not the discard mount option, which sends one on every delete (D4.2).
enable fstrim.timer
# systemd-pcrlock writes its policy into /var, and cryptenroll then uses it by itself: a disk sealed
# that way needs that file to open the place the file is on. Found by test: the disk would not open.
disable systemd-pcrlock-*
# The screen is the app; a login prompt on tty1 is text flashing past at boot.
disable getty@.service
# Started by medbrains-main.target once setup has finished, never before.
disable postgresql.service
# Only chrony.service may run: see mkosi.postinst.chroot.
disable chronyd-restricted.service
disable chrony-wait.service
# A kernel fix must never replace the boot loader on the way past: nothing could roll that back, and a
# power cut during it is the one write here with no second copy (OS-UPDATES.md).
disable systemd-boot-update.service
# Started by a udev rule only when a Wi-Fi card exists.
disable iwd.service
